  "aciklama": "TEOAE is the broadband response of the cochlea to a click stimulus. In this lesson we look at probe fit, the nonlinear click protocol, reproducibility with the A and B buffers, signal-to-noise ratio in frequency bands, sample pass rules, and the relationship between TEOAE and hearing loss.\n\nAIHEAR Audiology Academy makes short, clear lessons for audiology students and professionals.\n\nSources: Kemp DT (1978), Stimulated acoustic emissions from within the human auditory system, Journal of the Acoustical Society of America; Hall JW, Handbook of Otoacoustic Emissions; Dhar S, Hall JW, Otoacoustic Emissions: Principles, Procedures, and Protocols; Robinette MS, Glattke TJ, Otoacoustic Emissions: Clinical Applications; Katz, Handbook of Clinical Audiology.\n\nThis video is for educational purposes and does not replace diagnosis or treatment.",
