   "cumleler": [
    "Because the emission is so small, a single response is lost in the noise; so many responses are averaged.",
    "The device distributes the responses in turn into two separate memories, the A and B buffers.",
    "This gives two independent averages, recorded from the same ear over the same period.",
    "A true emission looks the same in both averages, while random noise differs between them.",
    "The difference between the two averages is used as an estimate of the noise, and their sum as an estimate of the response.",
    "Very noisy sweeps are excluded from the average by artifact rejection."
   ]
